# Cloud tiers — the offer

The companion to the pricing comparison directly above: having shown *we don't bill per seat*, this
section shows **what you actually choose** — how big a machine, and how much storage. Every tier is
the whole product (every feature, unlimited people); the only thing that changes up the ladder is
the size of the machine that's yours and the room it has for your data.

There is **no free tier** — a nexus is an always-on machine, so the floor is the smallest real
machine at **$20/mo**. The numbers are grounded in what the DeployKit provisions on Fly (an
always-on shared-CPU machine + a volume) at a healthy margin; the canonical, enforced tiers live in
`dogfood/nexus/deployment.work` (`Nexus.Config.tiers`), which the cloud control plane reads — this
section is the marketing mirror of those same numbers. Accents rotate the DNA pastels (sky · mint ·
peach · lilac), never the neon primary.

client :tiers do
